WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.787 --> 00:00:17.889
Mama refused to change her mind about tennis camp.

2
00:00:18.709 --> 00:00:24.652
But on Sunday night after Iris and Javier washed the dishes, they started begging her.

3
00:00:24.672 --> 00:00:28.054
"Can't we stay with a friend?"

4
00:00:28.654 --> 00:00:29.475
Iris pleaded.

5
00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:31.156
"Or a neighbor?"

6
00:00:31.788 --> 00:00:32.548
Javier said.

7
00:00:32.568 --> 00:00:36.869
"Mrs. Jones is always home, and she lives right downstairs."

8
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.150
Mama crossed her arms.

9
00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:42.531
"We can't impose on others like that."

10
00:00:43.611 --> 00:00:44.972
"What if Papa came home?"

11
00:00:45.672 --> 00:00:46.392
Iris asked.

12
00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:51.013
"Papa is not coming home, Iris," Mama said firmly.

13
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:56.055
"And even if he did, he could just as easily walk out again.

14
00:00:56.875 --> 00:00:58.675
We can't depend on anyone else."

15
00:00:59.676 --> 00:01:00.436
She shook her head.

16
00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.684
"You two are going to tennis camp tomorrow, and that's final."

17
00:01:05.704 --> 00:01:08.686
"Can Iris and I go to the park?"

18
00:01:09.186 --> 00:01:10.347
Javier blurted out.

19
00:01:11.288 --> 00:01:13.210
Iris and Mama both looked at him.

20
00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:18.254
"Javier never wants to go to the park," Iris thought.

21
00:01:18.274 --> 00:01:22.217
"It's getting late, Javier," Mama said.

22
00:01:22.817 --> 00:01:25.380
"You have to get up early for camp tomorrow morning."

23
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.103
"It's summertime," Javier said.

24
00:01:29.123 --> 00:01:32.660
"Please?" "Fine.

25
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:36.882
But stay together, and I want you back here in an hour."

26
00:01:36.902 --> 00:01:39.963
"No problem.

27
00:01:40.463 --> 00:01:41.424
Let's go, Iris."

28
00:01:42.164 --> 00:01:46.926
Javier waved Iris out the door, ignoring the confused look on her face.

29
00:01:51.028 --> 00:01:54.289
Once they were out in the hall, Iris poked her brother.

30
00:01:54.309 --> 00:01:56.570
"What's going on?"

31
00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:58.471
He shook his head.

32
00:01:58.491 --> 00:02:00.091
"At the park."

33
00:02:00.111 --> 00:02:04.225
"Fine." Iris followed him down the stairs.

34
00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:12.251
Outside, she jogged ahead, leaving Javier to try to keep up.

35
00:02:15.573 --> 00:02:20.057
She arrived at the park first and leaned against a bench to stretch her calves.

36
00:02:23.859 --> 00:02:28.763
A few moments later Javier flung himself on the bench, panting from his run.

37
00:02:31.864 --> 00:02:36.387
"We have to think of a way to get out of tennis camp.

38
00:02:37.228 --> 00:02:39.189
Mama's not going to change her mind."

39
00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:44.813
Iris had noticed a tennis court nearby and was watching some people play.

40
00:02:46.794 --> 00:02:49.316
"I think we're stuck playing tennis, Javier."

41
00:02:50.957 --> 00:02:52.158
Javier snorted.

42
00:02:52.178 --> 00:02:56.881
"I'd rather spend the week doing household chores than play tennis!"

43
00:02:58.002 --> 00:02:59.303
He squinted at the court.

44
00:02:59.323 --> 00:03:01.084
"Wait a minute.

45
00:03:02.044 --> 00:03:02.964
Is that Liam?"

46
00:03:03.985 --> 00:03:06.966
A kid from Javier's class waved and came over.

47
00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:11.548
"Hey, Javier," he said.

48
00:03:12.288 --> 00:03:16.030
Liam had a thick mop of red hair and a face full of freckles.

49
00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.890
"You're Iris, right?"

50
00:03:19.111 --> 00:03:19.831
Iris nodded.

51
00:03:20.832 --> 00:03:25.954
She and Javier were always in separate classes, but most of the kids at school knew they were

52
00:03:25.994 --> 00:03:29.875
twins. "Dude, since when do you play tennis?"

53
00:03:30.516 --> 00:03:31.376
Javier asked.

54
00:03:32.436 --> 00:03:33.337
Liam smiled.

55
00:03:33.357 --> 00:03:36.219
"My older sister, Molly, has been teaching me.

56
00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.481
She's on the high school team."

57
00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:43.385
"I taught him everything he knows."

58
00:03:44.326 --> 00:03:47.929
A taller, even brighter-haired version of Liam joined them.

59
00:03:47.949 --> 00:03:49.670
"I'm Molly."

60
00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:55.995
"Our mom signed us up for tennis camp," Javier said with a groan.

61
00:03:56.015 --> 00:03:58.377
"It starts tomorrow."

62
00:03:58.397 --> 00:04:01.980
"I'm really into soccer," Iris added.

63
00:04:02.644 --> 00:04:04.405
"I don't know anything about tennis."

64
00:04:04.425 --> 00:04:07.847
"Me neither," Javier said.

65
00:04:07.867 --> 00:04:10.168
"I can show you some of the basics."

66
00:04:10.989 --> 00:04:14.490
Molly handed Javier her racket and headed across the court.

67
00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:19.573
"Ball, racket, swing.

68
00:04:20.214 --> 00:04:21.634
That's all you need to know to start."

69
00:04:22.575 --> 00:04:26.297
Javier stepped onto the court and held the racket like a sword.

70
00:04:27.798 --> 00:04:33.581
When Molly hit the ball to him, he swung his racket in a wide arc, just tipping the

71
00:04:33.621 --> 00:04:36.242
ball, which dropped to the ground at his feet.

72
00:04:39.144 --> 00:04:43.446
He gave it several more tries before finally handing the racket back to Molly.

73
00:04:43.466 --> 00:04:49.549
"Thanks, but I stink at this," he said.

74
00:04:49.569 --> 00:04:51.010
"How about you?"

75
00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:52.711
Molly asked Iris.

76
00:04:53.731 --> 00:04:56.673
"It can't be that hard," Iris thought.

77
00:04:57.393 --> 00:04:59.635
After all, she was a good athlete.

78
00:05:00.795 --> 00:05:04.578
Iris took the racket and waited for Molly to serve a ball to her.

79
00:05:06.179 --> 00:05:09.141
Iris swung hard—and missed.

80
00:05:10.182 --> 00:05:13.084
The force of her swing spun her in a full circle.

81
00:05:13.764 --> 00:05:18.808
Javier laughed and so did Liam, though Liam quickly tried to cover it up.

82
00:05:21.349 --> 00:05:26.233
Heat spread up the back of Iris' neck as she tried to hit the ball again and again.

83
00:05:27.414 --> 00:05:32.413
Finally, after a particularly epic miss, everyone laughed hard.

84
00:05:35.194 --> 00:05:38.156
This time Iris herself had to join in.

85
00:05:38.176 --> 00:05:42.518
"Well, I stink at this too, Javier."

86
00:05:43.319 --> 00:05:45.160
She handed the racket back to Molly.

87
00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:49.622
"I guess my soccer skills aren't going to help me with tennis!"

88
00:05:50.422 --> 00:05:51.363
Liam shrugged.

89
00:05:52.163 --> 00:05:54.044
"I'm sure you'll learn to play at camp."

90
00:05:54.064 --> 00:05:56.926
"Yeah." Molly nodded.

91
00:05:56.946 --> 00:05:58.487
"Camp will be fun."

92
00:05:58.507 --> 00:06:00.408
"That reminds me."

93
00:06:01.088 --> 00:06:02.489
Javier nudged Iris.

94
00:06:02.509 --> 00:06:05.511
"We have some planning to do."

95
00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:07.913
He waved to Liam and Molly.

96
00:06:08.773 --> 00:06:14.097
"Later." The twins stepped off the court.

97
00:06:14.858 --> 00:06:17.660
"That was the worst," Javier said.

98
00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:20.061
Iris nodded glumly.

99
00:06:20.081 --> 00:06:24.404
"We have to get out of camp somehow," Javier went on.

100
00:06:24.424 --> 00:06:26.286
"Got any bright ideas?"

101
00:06:26.306 --> 00:06:29.308
"Not yet," Iris said.

102
00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:31.901
"But I'll try to think of something."

103
00:06:33.462 --> 00:06:38.003
The next morning the twins still had no plan for getting out of tennis camp.

104
00:06:39.024 --> 00:06:44.986
Mama was getting ready for work, but she had left out cereal and milk for breakfast, and bread

105
00:06:45.026 --> 00:06:47.367
and cheese for sandwiches to bring to camp.

106
00:06:48.188 --> 00:06:54.250
Javier drummed his fingers on the table as Iris slurped down her last mouthful of cereal.

107
00:06:58.112 --> 00:07:00.788
are we going to—" Javier froze.

108
00:07:01.669 --> 00:07:02.529
Iris looked up.

109
00:07:03.269 --> 00:07:07.070
Javier was staring at the bread and cheese next to their lunch bags.

110
00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:09.031
"I have an idea!"

111
00:07:09.711 --> 00:07:10.691
Javier grinned.

112
00:07:11.331 --> 00:07:12.552
"Just follow my lead.

113
00:07:13.252 --> 00:07:16.413
I'll make our lunches while you wash our breakfast dishes."

114
00:07:16.433 --> 00:07:20.534
"Huh?" Iris shot him a questioning look.

115
00:07:21.734 --> 00:07:28.496
Still, she carried the bowls to the sink and washed them while Javier prepared their sandwiches and water

116
00:07:28.536 --> 00:07:35.004
bottles. He was still busy when she went off to brush her teeth, but when she walked into

117
00:07:35.044 --> 00:07:39.487
the living room a few minutes later, their backpacks sat ready beside the front door.

118
00:07:40.388 --> 00:07:44.391
Javier slung his over his shoulder, and Iris did the same.

119
00:07:44.411 --> 00:07:47.174
"Ready to go to the bus stop?"

120
00:07:47.634 --> 00:07:48.515
Javier asked.

121
00:07:49.476 --> 00:07:53.439
"Yep." Mama stepped into the hallway and straightened her skirt.

122
00:07:53.459 --> 00:07:57.762
"I'm leaving for work in a few minutes."

123
00:07:58.603 --> 00:07:59.584
She blew them a kiss.

124
00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.101
"Have a good day at camp."

125
00:08:02.121 --> 00:08:04.682
"Bye," Iris said.

126
00:08:04.702 --> 00:08:08.524
"A good day would be a miracle," she thought.

127
00:08:08.544 --> 00:08:12.006
"You did what?"

128
00:08:13.107 --> 00:08:15.928
Iris turned to Javier once they'd reached the bus stop.

129
00:08:17.149 --> 00:08:21.171
"I thought leaving our lunches behind would be a good excuse for missing the bus."

130
00:08:21.972 --> 00:08:24.073
Javier wiped a hand over his forehead.

131
00:08:24.093 --> 00:08:27.995
"If we miss the bus, we can't go to camp, right?"

132
00:08:28.935 --> 00:08:29.936
Iris gasped.

133
00:08:30.652 --> 00:08:32.293
"Mama will be so mad!"

134
00:08:32.313 --> 00:08:34.574
"I know," Javier said.

135
00:08:34.594 --> 00:08:36.995
"But she'll be on her way to work.

136
00:08:37.775 --> 00:08:39.256
She might not even know."

137
00:08:39.276 --> 00:08:44.598
"Javier!" Iris was already speeding back toward the apartment building.

138
00:08:44.618 --> 00:08:48.179
"We have to get our lunches—now!"

139
00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:55.742
Just as Iris got to the front stoop, though, Mama stormed out the front door, their lunches in

140
00:08:55.782 --> 00:08:56.323
her hands.

141
00:08:56.343 --> 00:09:01.233
"You forgot your—" She halted.

142
00:09:01.773 --> 00:09:05.016
Iris and Javier followed Mama's gaze down the block.

143
00:09:05.836 --> 00:09:12.101
The camp bus was pulling away from the curb and picking up speed, leaving them behind.
